[38;5;252m[1m## Two harness issues worth knowing about[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C libraries reference each other ([38;5;10mcore_det[0m → [38;5;10mSPX_thash[0m, [38;5;10mlib<backend>[0m → [38;5;10mSPX_set_tree_index[0m), so loading them [38;5;10mRTLD_GLOBAL[0m was the obvious route — but that made the C definitions [1minterpose on the Rust cdylib's own exported globals[22m, so Rust's [38;5;10mrandombytes_init[0m was writing into C's [38;5;10mDRBG_ctx[0m. [38;5;10mbuild_c.sh[0m now links a stub [38;5;10mlibsphincs_all.so[0m whose [38;5;10mDT_NEEDED[0m order mirrors [38;5;10mtarget_link_libraries(driver sphincs_core_det ${HASH_BACKEND} crypto)[0m, opened [38;5;10mRTLD_LOCAL[0m so neither implementation can shadow the other.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mcrypto_sign_signature[0m draws [38;5;10moptrand[0m from the global DRBG, so the DRBG-dependent tests take a mutex and re-seed both libraries immediately before each call.[0m[0m
